#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054676 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054571 :question/id #uuid "92c02155-ad64-59a7-be4c-052e5bdfb429" :question/math-academy-id "e-6096" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f87e0eb91b6ec47ca8a4d64c2824396e613123ed37862975b606608ff70445f0.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=5-2x$." :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,5), B(2,1)$ and $C(3,0)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,5)$ results in a true statement:\n$y|= 5 - 2x; (5)|= 5 - 2(0); 5|= 5✓$\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line:\n- Substituting the point $B(2,1)$ results in a true statement:\n$y|= 5 - 2x; (1)|= 5 - 2(2); 1|= 1✓$\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line:\n- Substituting the point $C(3,0)$ results in a false statement:\n$y|= 5 - 2x; (0)|= 5 - 2(3); 0|=-1\\cdot$\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line:"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3123f8ed-a1ca-52b7-8427-2f3b60d9e68a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055125 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4e7efc6-2907-5146-bf87-e5dadaa7ef87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A, B$ and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052119} {:answer/id #uuid "113d6841-6789-509b-8adf-0487e9a14aed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052120} {:answer/id #uuid "25076717-a6b6-5e26-b5d4-9eeb494aa9c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052121} {:answer/id #uuid "7172bb65-a488-55f3-85a5-2a897483409f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052122} {:answer/id #uuid "798a3ace-bf62-53c2-b076-4cb83ba3fcf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text}